###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The dynamic cutoff changes how the neighbour graph is built; under the convention it is a setting on the run (cutoff-type, target-neighbors), and the four registry methods are reused. For dynamic runs cutoffRadius is the 6.0 A listed in the hyperparameter tables (the paper changes no hyperparameter other than the cutoff type).
# - Table 1 is read as one model per MD22 molecule (seven trainings per model and cutoff type); the paper says the models are 'trained on the MD22 dataset' and does not state the split sizes or whether the reported MAEs are validation or test. Table 1 values as printed: TensorNet dynamic on the buckyball catcher has force MAE 76.62 against 18.33 fixed; check against the PDF.
# - Mapping of the hyperparameter tables: MACE 'number of interactions' as numLayers, 'channels' as numFeatures, correlation order 2 as bodyOrder 3; Orb-v3 'message passing steps' as numLayers and 'latent dimension' as numFeatures; TensorNet 'number of units' as numFeatures. numEpochs is the maximum (early stopping applies).
# - The MatPES-r2SCAN node carries no reference calculation (r2SCAN is named only through the data-set name). NVE stability, melting simulations, memory and inference-time benchmarks (figures) and per-element force MAEs (Appendix F) are not encoded. Training hardware is stated only as '2 H100-80GB GPUs or 1 A6000 GPU, depending on batch size'.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
